WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.869
- I would go into agencies
and there would be closets of

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
computers and printers and
everything that they would do.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start position:0%
And so we started incentivizing
agencies to give money back

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.943
to the taxpayers.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.845
So you know, when
you go in there,

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.947
what they do is, "oh, we
need more people for this.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.448
We need more people for that."

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.617
You add a new program that's
not adding a person that's

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.386
adding 25 more people.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.921
That's the growth of government.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.456
And so at some point,

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.626
you go into every agency, you
look at every program and say,

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.194
what was the intent?

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.429
Is it still needed?

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.930
I did that in the
United Nations.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.634
I went into every single one
of the peacekeeping operations

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.935
we had.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.271
And I said, "what was
the original intent?"

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.305
Are we completing it?

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.274
And what's our exit strategy?

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.309
'Cause they had no exit
strategies to any of 'em.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
We saved $3 billion
the first year.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:50.583
It's just about putting some
good approaches in place that

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.319
make sure that they're actually
meeting the intended goal to

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.287
start with.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.588
And if there is no goal anymore,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.057
you scrap that program,

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
you scrap the people
that go with it.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.693
And that's how you
clean an agency.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.595
And then you go and
you put in something.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.197
Or anybody that's in a role,

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:97% position:3%
they can only serve in it four
to five years and then they

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:97% position:3%
roll to a different position
or another position.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.938
You never let 'em
sit for that long.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.108
(light ambient music)

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm Dave Rubin and
welcome to the first episode

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.983
of The Path to the Presidency.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.452
Over the coming months,

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.487
I'm gonna be interviewing all
of the declared Republican

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.089
presidential candidates.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.123
And if some Democrats get in,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.624
I guess we could do that too.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.094
And joining me to kick this
off is the former governor of

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.328
South Carolina,

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.897
the former US Ambassador
to the United Nations,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now Republican candidate
for president of the

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
United States, Nikki Haley,
Nikki, nice to see ya'.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:44.704
- Thanks for the chat.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.339
I appreciate it.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.907
- All right.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.210
You're first out of all of
the people, well you were,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.911 align:start size:88% position:13%
technically you weren't
first in, right?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.214
Donald Trump was first
in, you were second in,

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.949
but you're first with me,
which I would imagine is

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yes.
- Probably more important.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.220 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yes, you know, I mean,
look, I'm a decisive person.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.721
I didn't need to wait.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:03.289
I didn't need to wait to see
who else was gonna get in.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.025
I didn't need to wait or
worry about anything else.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.560
I think if you're gonna do this,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.529
you have to do it because you
know this is what you want and

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start position:0%
you know, this is what you think
you can do for the country.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.999
And so we were ready.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.267
And you know,

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.503
it's been a month and
it's been a whirlwind,

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:19.806
but we're working
and all is good.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What were the biggest
things holding you back before

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.577
announcing, or the
biggest worries,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'll get into the reasons
why you're running,

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.281
obviously, but like, what was
the stuff that you were going,

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.150
"ah, maybe I shouldn't do it."

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.684
- It's always only family.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.920
I mean, family's the only
reason that you, you know,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.824
you've got this when you,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.726
when you know you
can fix something,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.662
like it just itches at you.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.430
And really, after the midterms,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.665
I was like, that's it.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.033
That's it.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.301
You know, I mean,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.802
it's how much more do
you sit back and watch?

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.272 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I've always been a problem
solver and I know what we

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.706
need to do.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.608 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've been a two term governor
that took double digit

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
unemployment state and
turned it into an economic

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.279
powerhouse.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.813
I was at the UN, I didn't
deal with one country.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:04.384
I dealt with 193 and took the
kick me sign off of our back.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.520
And I look at where our country
is and I see us falling into

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:88% position:13%
this socialism and
defeatism and you know,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.659
there's not an avenue
that we don't have

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.893
serious issues with.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.396 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I'm thinking, you
know, I'm gonna do this.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.897
And you know,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.400
it goes back to the fact
that I look at my parents.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.237
They came here 50 years ago
when America was strong and

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.506
confident and full
of opportunities.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.309
I wanna prove to them that
they made the right decision.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.810
You know,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.545
I'm a military wife and I've
watched my husband and his

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.815
brothers and sisters go out
and fight for our freedoms.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.084 align:start size:88% position:13%
I want them to know
their sacrifice matter.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.586
Did it mean something?

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:42.255
And I look at my kids and my
daughter's getting married and

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.791
I see how hard it is
for her to buy a home.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.660
And my son is in college and
I see him writing papers he

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.631
doesn't believe in to get an A
and none of us should be okay

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.132
with that.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.735
And recently 50% of Americans
said that they don't think

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.438
their children will live
a better life than them.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.740 align:start size:97% position:3%
I refuse to let that happen
to this great country.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.275
I just refuse it.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.876
So I'm gonna get in there
and do something about it.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:06.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Are you shocked how
quickly things have changed?

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.747
For the worse?

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if you take
Trump's term before Covid

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.718
things were good.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.353
The economy was chugging along.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
We weren't in
extemporaneous wars,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.591
like things seemed
to be moving nicely.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.627
And then these last two years,

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
and especially just this last,
you know, week and a half,

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.930
with all of this banking stuff,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like everything
feels unsettled right now.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well when you have
a weak president,

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you have the most
socialist president

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.740 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we've ever had,
that's what's gonna happen.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, America's
not strong on our own.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.778
We have to actually work at it.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.714
And that's the part I hope
that Americans take away,

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
is it's gonna take every
single one of us to fix this.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.653
And in order to do that,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:49.088
you've gotta realize a lot
of things have gone wrong.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:52.759
And Dave, it wasn't just the
Democrats that did this to us.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.828
There are no Saint Republicans
right now because you look at

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.197
Congress and all
of this inflation,

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:97% position:3%
all the economic issues that
started with Republicans,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:06.306
that $2.2 trillion stimulus
package that was passed,

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.507
Republicans started it.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.842 align:start size:88% position:13%
Democrats have just
run with it after that.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then what did
Republicans do after that?

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:15.148
So first they do this free
for all, they expand welfare.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:18.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we now have 90 million
people on Medicare,

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:21.120
42 million people
on food stamps.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.489
So they expand welfare
and then, oh, it's bad.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.224
So what else do Republicans do?

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.427
Open up earmarks after 10 years.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:29.929
- So what do you make of that?

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.431
Because when every time,

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:33.966
so Republicans usually say
we're for small government,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.635
we're furlough taxes.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:38.037
And every now and again
someone does cut taxes.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.907 align:start size:97% position:3%
But when something like the
omnibus comes and they sign on

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:43.009
to all of these crazy
things and you know,

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
nobody's read the bill and
they know what we're all gonna

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:48.581
say about it, yet
they keep doing it.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.283
Is that to you,

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:52.085 align:start size:88% position:13%
just like the definition
of what the swamp is?

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:53.586
- I mean,

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.088
don't tell me that Republicans
and Democrats don't agree on

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:57.523
anything 'cause they love
to waste taxpayer money.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.758
- Right, right.

00:05:58.758 --> 00:05:59.959
- And they have no
value for a dollar.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's why I think we have
to have term limits.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.464 align:start position:0%
It's why I think we have to
have mandatory mental competency

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.099
tests over the age of 75.

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:07.934
I mean, this is serious.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.703
And then you look at the fact
that our debt is higher than

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:12.205
our economy.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.574
We're having to borrow money
to make our interest payments.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.376
I mean, none of this is okay.

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:19.412
And so Republicans love to
get on TV and talk about how

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.780
awful Biden is.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.181 align:start size:75% position:25%
They started it.
- Yeah.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.649
- So don't do that.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.251
But we can put an end to it.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.085
And that's the key.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.620
And you know,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.789
now they're looking at what's
gonna happen with the economy.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:32.458
And Biden of course wants
to just keep raising taxes.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.960
But what should they be doing?

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
Claw back the 500
billion in covid money

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.997
that hasn't been spent.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.800
Don't put IRS agents on
middle class Americans

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.269
go and get that a hundred
billion in covid fraud

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.470
that happened.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.874 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, if 15% of
our budget is interest,

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.542
stop borrowing money.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.777
We don't do that at home.

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.912
As governor, I had
to balance a budget.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:55.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
At what point is Congress
gonna realize they are not the

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:58.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
only body that gets exempt
from how they spend?

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:02.188
- Are you telling me if we
increase the deficit and

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.689
the ceiling,

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.025
the debt ceiling every year
or two years or whatever,

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:08.060
that that might cause
a long-term problem?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.429
Am I following you properly?

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.997
- I mean, look at
our households.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.532
- Yeah.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:14.033
- We don't spend more than
we make because we can't,

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.501
- It'd be pretty sweet if
you could just always up

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.702
that credit limit.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.204 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know, it's
amazing to me truly.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.907 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I mean Republicans can't
say they're conservative.

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.175
You're not conservative

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.676
if you're spending like that.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.912
And look, I've dealt with
that in South Carolina.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had a Republican house,
a Republican senate,

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.449
and they didn't see
anything they didn't,

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.317
that they didn't
love to spend on.

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:32.718
And we called 'em out on it.

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.320
We called out port projects,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.889
we called out the fact that
we had to pay down debt.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.357
We went and gave tax cuts.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:41.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like you've got to be
proactive and say enough.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:44.597 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think Republicans
have to realize, look, yeah,

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:46.365
we can bash the Democrats.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.533
They have been awful.

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.302 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're socialists,
it's terrible.

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.837
But let's look in the mirror.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:52.038
Look in the mirror.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.573
And Republicans in
Congress need to say,

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:56.209 align:start size:88% position:13%
but what responsibility
do we take?

00:07:56.209 --> 00:07:59.378
- Do you fear ever that
the cultural war has,

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.381
has been so lost that even
if you have all of the right

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:03.749
ideas, right,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.451 align:start size:97% position:3%
so we can talk about
individual rights and limited

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:07.153
government and free speech,

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:10.656 align:start position:0%
all of the right stuff that
the cultural part of this is so

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.859
messed up and so many people
don't understand what the real

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:15.428 align:start size:97% position:3%
issues are and kind of
just do want the government

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:16.662
to do everything.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.764
That it almost becomes
an unwinnable situation

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.765
for a Republican.

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:21.300
Like if you look
at the midterms,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.902
it's like the Republicans
obviously should have won.

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.504 align:start size:84% position:16%
And yet people were
basically like,

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
well the Democrats are
running everything.

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.640
It's not that good.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I'm not gonna
vote for a Republican.

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.810
- But I don't think
that's what happened.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.378 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, I endorsed
70 candidates,

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:35.214
we raised $10 million that
went directly into campaign

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:36.148
accounts.

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:37.550
I was on the ground campaigning.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.318
I think you had three
things that went wrong.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.786
I think first of all,

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
you saw Democrats out
raised Republicans again.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:45.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yep.
- You saw the fact that

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.492
Republicans have to get it out

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:47.860
of their heads.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.029 align:start size:84% position:16%
That you have to
vote on election day

