00:42:47.698 --> 00:42:50.301
you know, watching him,

00:42:50.301 --> 00:42:52.202
like he took a,

00:42:52.202 --> 00:42:56.473
did a total 180 and switched
on where he was on entitlements

00:42:56.473 --> 00:42:59.143
and is now where Trump is.

00:42:59.143 --> 00:43:02.012
He did a total 180 on where
he is with Ukraine and is now

00:43:02.012 --> 00:43:03.380
where Trump is.

00:43:03.380 --> 00:43:06.517 align:start size:88% position:13%
So it just comes across
like a Trump echo.

00:43:06.517 --> 00:43:08.018
Well, you know,

00:43:08.018 --> 00:43:09.653
then there's no difference
between the two of them.

00:43:09.653 --> 00:43:11.889
- Could some of that
just be being in office

00:43:11.889 --> 00:43:13.390
and how things change?

00:43:13.390 --> 00:43:16.694
- I'm not gonna assume to
know what he's thinking,

00:43:16.694 --> 00:43:18.128
why he's thinking it.

00:43:18.128 --> 00:43:21.198 align:start position:0%
I just think that it's odd
that he is literally saying the

00:43:21.198 --> 00:43:23.434 align:start size:97% position:3%
exact same things as Trump.
I mean, you see like,

00:43:23.434 --> 00:43:26.403
the same things are coming
out and I think Americans,

00:43:26.403 --> 00:43:28.072 align:start size:88% position:13%
when they look at it,
it's out where the case,

00:43:28.072 --> 00:43:29.006
they just vote for Trump.

00:43:29.006 --> 00:43:30.240
They're not looking for an echo.

00:43:30.240 --> 00:43:33.110
They're looking for
like, for options.

00:43:33.110 --> 00:43:34.645
But, you know,

00:43:34.645 --> 00:43:36.146
he's gotta decide where he
is gonna be on everything.

00:43:36.146 --> 00:43:38.716
I think you have to be honest
with the American people and

00:43:38.716 --> 00:43:41.318 align:start position:0%
say, yes, you've gotta
acknowledge entitlement reforms,

00:43:41.318 --> 00:43:42.586
but there's a way to do it.

00:43:42.586 --> 00:43:44.488
I think you've gotta
be honest on, you know,

00:43:44.488 --> 00:43:46.590
foreign policy that, look,

00:43:46.590 --> 00:43:49.259
if you are gonna be weak
in the knees on Russia,

00:43:49.259 --> 00:43:51.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're gonna end up with
Russia being just like China.

00:43:51.762 --> 00:43:53.197
We've watched that happen.

00:43:53.197 --> 00:43:55.366 align:start position:0%
We had republicans and Democrats
that got weak in the knees

00:43:55.366 --> 00:43:57.034
on China and said,
oh, just leave them,

00:43:57.034 --> 00:43:59.136
if we're nice to them,
they'll wanna be like us.

00:43:59.136 --> 00:44:01.872 align:start position:0%
That is why we are in this
situation where they're stealing

00:44:01.872 --> 00:44:03.674
intellectual property.

00:44:03.674 --> 00:44:05.142
They're now in our universities.

00:44:05.142 --> 00:44:06.877
They're buying up our farmland.

00:44:06.877 --> 00:44:08.779 align:start size:88% position:13%
They're sending spy
balloons up in the air.

00:44:08.779 --> 00:44:10.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
It all started
with people saying,

00:44:10.714 --> 00:44:12.583
you don't need to
worry about China.

00:44:12.583 --> 00:44:14.084
Let's just worry about us.

00:44:14.084 --> 00:44:16.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, you start doing
that with Russia,

00:44:16.153 --> 00:44:18.122
and now you're gonna have
China and Russia there.

00:44:18.122 --> 00:44:19.556
- So actually,

00:44:19.556 --> 00:44:20.791 align:start size:97% position:3%
instead of with our remaining
time going through the,

00:44:20.791 --> 00:44:22.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
the laundry list of
people that are running,

00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:24.228
I think those are the big two.

00:44:24.228 --> 00:44:25.229
So, all right.

00:44:25.229 --> 00:44:26.430
Your feelings are clear on that.

00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:27.898 align:start size:88% position:13%
I just wanna ask you
sort of philosophically,

00:44:27.898 --> 00:44:29.433 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think one of the things
that I'm seeing bubble up now

00:44:29.433 --> 00:44:33.470
constantly is that the people
feel that the machine itself,

00:44:33.470 --> 00:44:36.607
that the way the United
States was constructed

00:44:36.607 --> 00:44:38.175
cannot work at a federal level.

00:44:38.175 --> 00:44:41.011
That the states are so out of
whack with each other and that

00:44:41.011 --> 00:44:42.613
I fled California, that I,

00:44:42.613 --> 00:44:45.115
I truly see no hope for
after the last time I was

00:44:45.115 --> 00:44:45.949
in San Francisco.

00:44:45.949 --> 00:44:47.184
I mean, it is,

00:44:47.184 --> 00:44:48.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
it barely looks like
an American city.

00:44:48.819 --> 00:44:50.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
It looks like a third
world country, basically.

00:44:50.688 --> 00:44:51.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Very sad.
- And then I see how

00:44:51.955 --> 00:44:53.424
things are flourishing here,

00:44:53.424 --> 00:44:55.526 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there really is a feeling
amongst a certain set of

00:44:55.526 --> 00:44:56.360
people on the right.

00:44:56.360 --> 00:44:57.828
Like actually the,

00:44:57.828 --> 00:45:01.065
the united part of this thing
is not gonna work anymore.

00:45:01.065 --> 00:45:03.033
And that we should only
focus on the states.

00:45:03.033 --> 00:45:03.967
What do you think about that?

00:45:03.967 --> 00:45:05.202
- I'm a states rights girl.

00:45:05.202 --> 00:45:07.071
You know, I mean, I think that,

00:45:07.071 --> 00:45:08.639
you know, as a governor,

00:45:08.639 --> 00:45:11.442
I think that the majority
of control should always be

00:45:11.442 --> 00:45:12.676
in the states.

00:45:12.676 --> 00:45:14.378
I mean, look, the
federal government,

00:45:14.378 --> 00:45:15.679
it breaks more than it fixes.

00:45:15.679 --> 00:45:17.214
We see that every day.

00:45:17.214 --> 00:45:18.849
So, you know, as president,

00:45:18.849 --> 00:45:21.485
my goal is gonna be
to empower the states

00:45:21.485 --> 00:45:22.820
as much as possible.

00:45:22.820 --> 00:45:24.722
Whether it's healthcare,
whether it's education,

00:45:24.722 --> 00:45:27.157 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's military, whether
it's all of those things.

00:45:27.157 --> 00:45:29.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's best when it's
closest to the people.

00:45:29.493 --> 00:45:31.628 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's when government
runs the best.

00:45:31.628 --> 00:45:35.332
When you have these behemoth
agencies that get so bloated

00:45:35.332 --> 00:45:36.834
and so big,

00:45:36.834 --> 00:45:39.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then try and dictate to
everybody what they should do,

00:45:39.236 --> 00:45:40.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think that's part
of the problem.

00:45:40.771 --> 00:45:42.239
We've gotta clean it out.

00:45:42.239 --> 00:45:43.474
- What does that mean?

00:45:43.474 --> 00:45:44.742
Like, to like,

00:45:44.742 --> 00:45:46.243
'cause I think there's
gonna be a competition

00:45:46.243 --> 00:45:47.711
for you guys to basically
blow apart every agency.

00:45:47.711 --> 00:45:49.213
I can see it happening on stage.

00:45:49.213 --> 00:45:50.814
How many of you will blow
apart the department of Ed?

00:45:50.814 --> 00:45:53.117
How many are part like
EPA, blah blah, blah?

00:45:53.117 --> 00:45:54.752 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, is that
what you'd go for?

00:45:54.752 --> 00:45:56.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like really just like
dissembling these things?

00:45:56.987 --> 00:45:59.990
- So what I did in
South Carolina was I
made sure that I put

00:45:59.990 --> 00:46:02.926 align:start size:97% position:3%
people in charge of those
agencies and put people within

00:46:02.926 --> 00:46:03.861
those agencies.

00:46:03.861 --> 00:46:05.596
Their job was to clean it up,

00:46:05.596 --> 00:46:08.499
get rid of the red tape,
get rid of the bureaucracy,

00:46:08.499 --> 00:46:11.068
get rid of the people who had
been there too long that had

00:46:11.068 --> 00:46:13.170
created these power fiefdoms.

00:46:13.170 --> 00:46:17.374
And just in some agencies it
required really cleaning house

00:46:17.374 --> 00:46:19.443
and some it required tweaks.

00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:20.377
But you don't know, you know,

00:46:20.377 --> 00:46:21.912
once you get in there,

00:46:21.912 --> 00:46:24.248
but you have to assume they
all are bloated and they all

00:46:24.248 --> 00:46:25.783
have it.

00:46:25.783 --> 00:46:28.051
And it should be a number one
priority that you do day one,

00:46:28.051 --> 00:46:28.986
that that's in there.

00:46:28.986 --> 00:46:30.487
And that's the number one rule.

00:46:30.487 --> 00:46:32.990
Because if you don't have
a government that works

00:46:32.990 --> 00:46:34.691
for the people,

00:46:34.691 --> 00:46:38.061 align:start size:84% position:16%
then you've just got
a government that
works for power and

00:46:38.061 --> 00:46:39.530
that's what you don't want.

00:46:39.530 --> 00:46:42.099
The second part is we've
gotta get to a place where,

00:46:42.099 --> 00:46:46.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much as I love term
limits within bureaucracy,

00:46:46.170 --> 00:46:48.005
you've gotta roll people over.

00:46:48.005 --> 00:46:50.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
No one should stay in the
same job for 20 or 30 years.

00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:52.409
- Is that in essence
what the deep state,

00:46:52.409 --> 00:46:53.644
when people say deep state,

00:46:53.644 --> 00:46:55.112
is that what they mean
more than anything else?

00:46:55.112 --> 00:46:57.281 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's just the bureaucratic
layer of these people that are

00:46:57.281 --> 00:47:00.384
sort of never moving
in these agencies.

00:47:00.384 --> 00:47:01.919
So the president comes and goes,

00:47:01.919 --> 00:47:04.454
but these guys are 40 years
in doing the same thing and

00:47:04.454 --> 00:47:05.522
making awful lot
of money doing it.

00:47:05.522 --> 00:47:06.990
- Well, you know,

00:47:06.990 --> 00:47:08.659 align:start position:0%
it's like when I was at the
United Nations and I was going,

00:47:08.659 --> 00:47:11.929
my first speech was actually
hitting Russia on what they

00:47:11.929 --> 00:47:13.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
were doing with
Ukraine at the time

00:47:13.063 --> 00:47:14.598
and the whole Crimea thing.

00:47:14.598 --> 00:47:18.936
And so when I went in, you
know, I drafted my speech,

00:47:18.936 --> 00:47:21.572
I was ready to go, I sent
it to the State Department,

00:47:21.572 --> 00:47:23.106
you know,

00:47:23.106 --> 00:47:23.941
just in National Security
Council so that they could

00:47:23.941 --> 00:47:25.442
look it over.

00:47:25.442 --> 00:47:28.846
They called back all upset
saying, you can't say this.

00:47:28.846 --> 00:47:30.414
And I said, well, what part?

00:47:30.414 --> 00:47:33.016
You know, what part's
factually incorrect?

00:47:33.016 --> 00:47:34.685 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they said, well, none
of it's factually incorrect,

00:47:34.685 --> 00:47:36.987
but you can't talk like this.

00:47:36.987 --> 00:47:38.222
And I said, okay,

00:47:38.222 --> 00:47:40.891
if you've got an issue
or a fact, it is wrong.

00:47:40.891 --> 00:47:42.893
I am the first one
to wanna fix it.

00:47:42.893 --> 00:47:46.530 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can't tell me
how to say something.

00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:48.832 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I just ignored 'em
and I went forward.

00:47:48.832 --> 00:47:51.602 align:start size:97% position:3%
But that's kind of, they
want you to do it their way.

00:47:51.602 --> 00:47:53.070
They want you to do things.

00:47:53.070 --> 00:47:54.571
But you know,

00:47:54.571 --> 00:47:56.273
the reason that I was able
to do so much in the United

00:47:56.273 --> 00:47:58.442
Nations was I went
in with fresh eyes.

00:47:58.442 --> 00:47:59.943
You know,

00:47:59.943 --> 00:48:03.247
I went in and really wanted
to break what needed to be

00:48:03.247 --> 00:48:06.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
broken and see it
through a different lens.

00:48:06.183 --> 00:48:09.486
And I've never held office in
DC but I think that same thing

00:48:09.486 --> 00:48:10.954
needs to happen.

00:48:10.954 --> 00:48:14.291
You've gotta go in and not
have allegiances to anything.

00:48:14.291 --> 00:48:16.760
You've gotta build it,
build the trust back up.

00:48:16.760 --> 00:48:20.497 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, Americans
don't trust any agency.

00:48:20.497 --> 00:48:23.066 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- And so the number one

00:48:23.066 --> 00:48:25.269
goal of a leader
is Americans should

00:48:25.269 --> 00:48:28.305
at least trust what these
agencies are telling them.

00:48:28.305 --> 00:48:31.775
And if they're so big and so
bureaucratic and so powerful,

00:48:31.775 --> 00:48:33.911
something's wrong
with the system.

00:48:33.911 --> 00:48:35.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Would you say
that's all a result

00:48:35.779 --> 00:48:38.215 align:start size:84% position:16%
of just sort of
bipartisan bad policy?

00:48:38.215 --> 00:48:40.217 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or is that really
just this, you know,

00:48:40.217 --> 00:48:41.652
we did 50 some odd minutes.

00:48:41.652 --> 00:48:43.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
We haven't said
the word woke once.

00:48:43.153 --> 00:48:46.790
Like is it just that wokeness
has now infected everything

00:48:46.790 --> 00:48:50.093 align:start size:97% position:3%
and all of the wrong people
are being hired for all of the

00:48:50.093 --> 00:48:52.195
wrong thing, all of
the wrong reasons,

00:48:52.195 --> 00:48:54.665
and nobody's qualified
to do any of this anyway.

00:48:54.665 --> 00:48:55.866 align:start size:84% position:16%
- This was before
any of the wokeness.

00:48:55.866 --> 00:48:57.100
- Yeah,

00:48:57.100 --> 00:48:59.202 align:start size:84% position:16%
- This was the fact
that, you know,

00:48:59.202 --> 00:49:00.671
I saw this in South Carolina.

00:49:00.671 --> 00:49:03.674 align:start size:97% position:3%
Agencies think that if they're
gonna get the same budget

00:49:03.674 --> 00:49:05.208
next year,

00:49:05.208 --> 00:49:07.210
they have to spend everything
that they have and we put in,

00:49:07.210 --> 00:49:08.645
- It's true, right?

00:49:08.645 --> 00:49:09.613 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not just that they
think it, it's actually true.

00:49:09.613 --> 00:49:10.948
- It's true.

00:49:10.948 --> 00:49:12.416
- I wish I could remember this.

00:49:12.416 --> 00:49:13.884
- I would go into agencies
and there would be closets of

00:49:13.884 --> 00:49:15.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
computers and printers and
everything that they would do.

00:49:15.752 --> 00:49:19.323
And so we start incentivizing
agencies to give money back to

00:49:19.323 --> 00:49:20.557
the taxpayers.

00:49:20.557 --> 00:49:22.459
So you know, when
you go in there,

00:49:22.459 --> 00:49:24.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
what they do is, oh, we
need more people for this.

00:49:24.594 --> 00:49:26.096
We need more people for that.

00:49:26.096 --> 00:49:28.231
You add a new program that's
not adding a person that's

00:49:28.231 --> 00:49:30.000
adding 25 more people.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.602
That's the growth of government.

00:49:32.602 --> 00:49:35.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so at some point,
you go into every agency,

00:49:35.505 --> 00:49:38.809 align:start size:97% position:3%
you look at every program
and say, what was the intent?

00:49:38.809 --> 00:49:40.043
Is it still needed?

00:49:40.043 --> 00:49:41.545
I did that in the
United Nations.

00:49:41.545 --> 00:49:44.915
I went into every single one
of the peacekeeping operations

00:49:44.915 --> 00:49:46.216
we had.

00:49:46.216 --> 00:49:48.385
And I said, what was
the original intent?

00:49:48.385 --> 00:49:49.886
Are we completing it?

00:49:49.886 --> 00:49:51.455
And what's our exit strategy?

00:49:51.455 --> 00:49:53.924
Because they had no exit
strategies to any of 'em.

00:49:53.924 --> 00:49:57.194 align:start size:81% position:19%
We saved 3 billion
the first year.

00:49:57.194 --> 00:50:01.198
It's just about putting some
good approaches in place that

00:50:01.198 --> 00:50:03.900
make sure that they're actually
meeting the intended goal to

00:50:03.900 --> 00:50:04.835
start with.

00:50:04.835 --> 00:50:06.203
And if there is no goal anymore,

00:50:06.203 --> 00:50:07.637
you scrap that program,

00:50:07.637 --> 00:50:09.006 align:start size:84% position:16%
you scrap the people
that go with it,

00:50:09.006 --> 00:50:11.375
and that's how you
clean an agency.

00:50:11.375 --> 00:50:13.276
And then you go and
you put in something.

00:50:13.276 --> 00:50:14.911
Or anybody that's in a role,

00:50:14.911 --> 00:50:17.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
they can only serve in it four
to five years and then they

00:50:17.714 --> 00:50:19.950 align:start size:97% position:3%
roll to a different position
or another position.

00:50:19.950 --> 00:50:22.219
You never let 'em
sit for that long.

00:50:22.219 --> 00:50:24.454
- So speaking of the UN quickly,

00:50:24.454 --> 00:50:27.891
is it weird to you how
irrelevant the UN is now?

00:50:27.891 --> 00:50:30.227
I mean, it almost is like
in complete conjunction

00:50:30.227 --> 00:50:34.197
with you leaving like the UN
is, no one talks about the UN.

00:50:34.197 --> 00:50:36.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
They don't, it doesn't seem
like they meet anymore.

00:50:36.166 --> 00:50:37.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
Does the security
council do anything?

00:50:37.768 --> 00:50:39.536 align:start size:88% position:13%
Do they even know what's
happening in Russia?

00:50:39.536 --> 00:50:41.071
Like what is the
UN at this point,

00:50:41.071 --> 00:50:43.206
except that they rack up
a lot of parking tickets?

00:50:43.206 --> 00:50:44.174
- No, the UN is a farce.

00:50:44.174 --> 00:50:45.375
I've said that for a long time.

00:50:45.375 --> 00:50:46.643 align:start size:84% position:16%
But what's interesting
you say that is

00:50:46.643 --> 00:50:49.846
I was meeting with Prime
Minister Modi in India

00:50:49.846 --> 00:50:51.381
back when I was at the UN.

00:50:51.381 --> 00:50:54.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we were talking about
at the time their alliances,

00:50:54.918 --> 00:50:56.453
you know,

00:50:56.453 --> 00:50:57.988
their military cooperation
with Russia at the time.

00:50:57.988 --> 00:50:59.489
And he said, do you know,

00:50:59.489 --> 00:51:01.458
I never paid attention
to the United Nations

00:51:01.458 --> 00:51:03.293
until you were there.

00:51:03.293 --> 00:51:07.531
But the reason that was the
case was it wasn't about me

00:51:07.531 --> 00:51:09.032
specifically,

00:51:09.032 --> 00:51:10.767
it was about the fact that
I forced them to talk about

00:51:10.767 --> 00:51:12.803 align:start size:97% position:3%
things that were
uncomfortable to talk about.

00:51:12.803 --> 00:51:15.338
I forced them to deal with
issues of the day and not old

00:51:15.338 --> 00:51:16.807
archaic things.

00:51:16.807 --> 00:51:19.209 align:start position:0%
And I called them out when they
were doing something wrong.

00:51:19.209 --> 00:51:22.112
And you know, just said, why
aren't we talking about Russia?

00:51:22.112 --> 00:51:24.314 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why aren't we talking about
the chemical weapons in Syria?

00:51:24.314 --> 00:51:26.083
Why aren't we talking
about the Iran deal

00:51:26.083 --> 00:51:27.551
and how they're violating?

